  "_notes": [
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 NO MONEY MOVES. paymentType is not a tender — no gateway, no amount, no result. It is an INSTRUCTION to OMS that the customer wants to pay before delivery, on which OMS sends them a payment-gateway link. A routing flag on the document, in the same family as documentSource, which is why it creates no price-affecting power.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 IT IS AN INDEPENDENT AXIS. All four combinations are legal (owner ruling 2026-07-29: 'it's not linked with deliveryType — any order could be paid online or cash on delivery'). What this replaced, CallCenterSessionService.Submit's `CashOnDelivery = isDelivery`, took the value off an unrelated axis and was wrong BOTH ways — and it was stamping values nobody chose onto real documents.",
    "The flip leaves plant, lines and totals byte-identical INCLUDING totals.deliveryFee: the fee predicate has no payment term, and a capture is the cheapest place to keep it that way.",
    "\uD83D\uDEA9 Receivable is RESERVED: a legal COLUMN value ('R' in DocumentPaymentTypeConstants, so the domain is three-valued and adding it later is data rather than a schema change) and a REFUSED request. It is named on the wire so adding it later is not a §9 major, not because any phase-1 path may set it.",
    "⚠ ONLINE IS 'O', NOT 'P' — 'P' is PickInStore on the DELIVERY axis. The wire spells the words; the column keeps C / O / R. Storing 'P' as a payment type would push a value SAP does not recognise onto a real order, and nothing downstream validates the domain, so it would land silently.",
    "canChangePaymentType is TRUE on every phase-1 order and paymentTypeForcedReason is NULL — a negative assertion, deliberately. 155 found the premise for a forcing rule wrong (P2E online-forcing is a KIND rule; DocumentSourcePolicyService forces only delivery-only, which is 826's axis), so it is built as a server-side lookup that answers 'no rule' rather than a hard-coded source list.",
    "There is no lines-exist gate on setPaymentType: nothing moves.",
    "setOrderNote is free text onto the CLCN header — CC2 carries OrderNote on its main VM and it was never charted. null CLEARS it; the column is NVARCHAR(MAX) so a long note is not silently truncated at 8000."
  ]
}
